{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292779-shaping-rituals-and-sorcerous-initiations","id":1292779,"title":"Shaping Rituals and Sorcerous Initiations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-28T08:46:08-08:00","id":1292779,"title":"Shaping Rituals and Sorcerous Initiations","content":"Y'all should know by now I'm a big sorcery fan. After the release of the Lunar sorcery stuff this Tuesday I decided there's finally enough material out there between the Core book, the Dragon-blooded book, and the Lunars book to just compile everything into a single document... which I did. Since it's copy-pasted from the books, I'm pretty sure I can't post it here. BUT it got me looking more deeply at comparing, contrasting, and just generally thinking about Shaping Rituals and Sorcerous Initiations.<br /> <br /> Here's what we have so far:<br /> <b>Core book</b><ul><li>Bargain with Mara</li> <li>Pact with an Ifrit Lord</li> <li>Scarred by Nightmares</li> <li>Soul-Perfecting Elixir</li> <li>The Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes</li> </ul><b>Dragon-Blooded book</b><ul><li>Student of the Heptagram</li> <li>Wanasaan Exorcist</li> </ul><b>Lunars book</b><ul><li>Raksi's Tutelage</li> <li>The Jasmine Gems of Mishiko</li> <li>Root-Lore</li> </ul>My favorite Initiation is easily the <i>Pact with an Ifrit Lord</i>, and my favorite Shaping Ritual is drawing motes from a source of fire. Its a great source of stunt fodder when shaping spells, and I've even used it strategically at the start of combat by snuffing out all the candles in a room so my spell casts in sudden darkness.<br /> <br /> As my fire-breaking Twilight approaches Essence 3, I am compelled to consider how he should initiate into the Celestial Circle. I'm leaning towards The Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes (all around useful) or the Soul-Perfecting Elixir (mostly for the merits) but I find some fun stuff in all of them.<br /> <br /> So what are YOUR favorite Shaping rituals and Sorcerous Initiations? Why do you like them? Have they inspired some interesting new homebrew? Tell me about them! Constructive criticism about particular Initiations or Rituals is permitted, but this is largely a positive thread about Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T09:08:41-08:00","id":1292783,"title":"","content":"Sorcerer's harvest from Root Lore is basically a Wood-element version of the first shaping ritual of Pact with an Ifrit Lord (which I just realised has no name. None of the corebook rituals do.)<br /> <br /> So I kind of want to come up with initiations that include water, earth and air versions of the idea now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T09:45:28-08:00","id":1292795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292779-shaping-rituals-and-sorcerous-initiations?p=1292783#post1292783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerer's harvest from Root Lore is basically a Wood-element version of the first shaping ritual of Pact with an Ifrit Lord (which I just realised has no name. None of the corebook rituals do.)<br /> <br /> So I kind of want to come up with initiations that include water, earth and air versions of the idea now.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a minor effort at this back when the first backer preview of the core book came out a few years back. I always think it's worth the effort. Though mostly it was aimed with reskinning The Burning Name to different elements, it has a broad scope of appeal among the other merits as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T09:48:27-08:00","id":1292796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292779-shaping-rituals-and-sorcerous-initiations?p=1292783#post1292783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerer's harvest from Root Lore is basically a Wood-element version of the first shaping ritual of Pact with an Ifrit Lord (which I just realised has no name. None of the corebook rituals do.)<br /> <br /> So I kind of want to come up with initiations that include water, earth and air versions of the idea now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally, I just realized that Sorcerer's Harvest, in direct comparison to the Pact equivalent is possibly objectively worse. You can only draw from each source once per day, whereas you can draw from the same source (provided it's large enough) multiple times with the Pact version for the same number of motes. Thoughts on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T09:51:07-08:00","id":1292797,"title":"","content":"It's probably because it doesn't diminish the plants and it's a lot less dangerous to stand in a forest than in a bonfire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T10:10:21-08:00","id":1292802,"title":"","content":"And you're more likely to be standing near a plant than some fire.<br /> <br /> For water, the Wanasaan initiation has a ritual where you submerge yourself in saltwater.<br /> I could well imagine an aquamancer meditating under a waterfall or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T11:20:12-08:00","id":1292817,"title":"","content":"I made a Solar Sorcerer initiation by taking an inverted piece of Mara's initiation, pieces of the Pact with an Ifrit Lord, and the merits of the Mice of the Sun to create the &quot;Covenant of the Sun&quot;, which drew some inspiration from <i>Dark Souls'</i> Warrior of Sunlight Covenant.<br /> <br /> I did not write up Sunlight Spear as a spell.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T12:01:30-08:00","id":1292823,"title":"","content":"I think my favourite initiation and shaping ritual is the Heptagram and Sevenfold Art Invocation, just for the classic Doctor Strange calling on mystical powers beyond space and time with precise thought, action and words.<br /> <br /> In fact I\u2019ve been thinking of adapting the spells seen in the movies into Exalted sorcereries if anyone would be interested in seeing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T12:40:53-08:00","id":1292831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292779-shaping-rituals-and-sorcerous-initiations?p=1292823#post1292823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my favourite initiation and shaping ritual is the Heptagram and Sevenfold Art Invocation, just for the classic Doctor Strange calling on mystical powers beyond space and time with precise thought, action and words.<br /> <br /> In fact I\u2019ve been thinking of adapting the spells seen in the movies into Exalted sorcereries if anyone would be interested in seeing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would enjoy seeing that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T13:24:07-08:00","id":1292844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292779-shaping-rituals-and-sorcerous-initiations?p=1292823#post1292823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my favourite initiation and shaping ritual is the Heptagram and Sevenfold Art Invocation, just for the classic Doctor Strange calling on mystical powers beyond space and time with precise thought, action and words.<br /> <br /> In fact I\u2019ve been thinking of adapting the spells seen in the movies into Exalted sorcereries if anyone would be interested in seeing that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd love to see that too. And now makes me think we need to see initiations based on having the Infinity Gauntlet and the various stones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T14:20:47-08:00","id":1292854,"title":"","content":"I was happy to find that the Bargain with Mara initiation had themes and benefits that allowed me to simulate an Infernal sorcerer/swordsman (inspired by Yrkoon) using the core rules. That ritual that involves stealing the souls of people you seduce and exchanging them for power reminded me of the way Melniboneans were depicted sacrificing slaves to fuel sorcery in <i>Michael Moorcock's Elric Vol. 1: The Ruby Throne</i>, and dovetails with the character's background as a son of privilege from Ysyr. The Infernal Nobility merit in particular should come in quite handy for a sorcerer who interacts a lot with demons, and I love the aesthetics of demonic tattoos even though I wasn't able to do anything practical with them at chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T14:51:58-08:00","id":1292860,"title":"","content":"The corebook had a shaping ritual based on strong weather that could work as an air-aspected version","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T21:46:25-08:00","id":1292941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292779-shaping-rituals-and-sorcerous-initiations?p=1292802#post1292802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you're more likely to be standing near a plant than some fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you, some kinda coward who's afraid of arson?<br /> I'm refluffing Root-Lore for a rat-shape Lunar sorcerer who's more of a city rat. They dig around in the trash and find some old chicken feet, and then later it turns out that old chicken feet is exactly what they needed to cast Flight of Separation. Or they never end up using it, and they get a free snack of chicken feet instead. Improvise, adapt, overcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T00:32:46-08:00","id":1292962,"title":"","content":"I really like Scarred by the Nightmares from the Core book. I picked both Terrestrial and Celestial shaping rituals from it, so my Twilight has a Derangement and can leech off emotions.<br /> She believes an unshaped raksha is living in her head and that it is actually the one performing the sorcery. Running out of Willpower causes this other personality to manifest.<br /> <br /> I've told my ST that I don't know, whether my Twilight really has a raksha in her mind or if she's just delusional. But he's free to choose either way, if it serves the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","name":"Taleksi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T17:31:28-08:00","id":1293195,"title":"","content":"My favorite would be The Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes, just because I really like the idea of sorcerous artifacts like that. Bargain with Mara is really fun with the demonic tattoos too, but the shaping rituals for that one aren't great for the characters I tend to play.<br /> <br /> Though now that we have Raksi's Tutelage, that might actually be one of my new favorites. Both nice merits and shaping rituals.<br /> <br /> I've actually played sorcerers with the Talisman initiation, as well as one with a homebrew sorcerous artifact that was basically just Jafar's staff from the Disney Alladin movie, and I had one kind of weird sorcerer who had an entirely homebrewed initiation involving their split personality (their personalities were at odds a lot, but could commit motes to grant the other personality sorcerous motes when they switched control)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T17:37:08-08:00","id":1293377,"title":"","content":"Has anyone tried comparing the various sorcerous mote rewards from the shaping rituals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T19:25:54-08:00","id":1293631,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Sorcery is one of my favourite things too, especially 3e sorcery. My Twilight made a bet with Sigereth and won Terrestrial initiation.<br /> <br /> I took Infernal Nobility from Mara's initiation and wrote these:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>(Something)</b> \u2013 (I didn't actually take this one, it's just an idea) It is forbidden to win by cheating. The sorceror automatically gains 3 successes on contested rolls to perceive mundane cheating, or double 8s on rolls to perceive supernaturally-concealed cheating. (This power enhances other effects that pierce supernatural obfuscation, it grants no special power to contest supernatural powers on its own.) At the Storyteller's discretion, this power can also apply to \u201ccheating\u201d in a more metaphorical sense \u2013 perceiving ambushes or other surprise tactics in war, subtle sabotage of occult efforts, etc.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Gambler's Silver Tongue (3) </b>- Cheating may be forbidden, but cunning is all part of the game. This merit allows a character to substitute their Larceny rating for more relevant social abilities if the roll pertains to games or gambling. The most obvious application is to substitute Larceny for Socialise when trying to bluff, or make/resist a read intentions roll from a character they're trying to convince to make a bet, but the character may find stranger uses, i.e. using Larceny in lieu of Performance when flair shuffling. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">(Then I convinced the other PCs and a demon to bet on a game of Gateway, and the ST used some homebrew system involving 3 rolls for 3 stages of the game, the first of which was Socialise. I forgot to invoke Gambler's Silver Tongue.) Because I didn't take the first one, we didn't seriously examine it. It probably isn't balanced right, it feels off to me.<br /> <br /> My ST came up with these shaping rituals:</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As part of a shape sorcery action, the sorcerer offers up an object as a bet and asks for a number of sorcerous motes (maximum of 5), then rolls (Manipulation + Larceny, difficulty 1+ the number of motes asked for minus the resources of the object). On a success, the requested sorcerous motes are gained. On a failure, the object is immediately sucked into Sigereth's domain. The object has to be something that is considered owned by the sorcerer, but does not have to be present. Intimacies can be bid as well, with their strength substituting for the resources rating. If an Intimacy is lost, all memory of the subject is lost as well, though the subject itself remains. Each wager only be gambled once per scene, except when casting the sorcerer's control spell, when repeated gamblings of the same wager in a scene add 1 to the difficulty each time. The sorcerer cannot draw more than ten sorcerous motes per scene with this ritual.<br /> <br /> While playing a game of chance or skill, the sorcerer can invite another mortal player to stake themselves on the outcome. The mortal can not be compelled to place the bet, nor can they be compelled to lose the game, but other persuasion is acceptable. No stipulations are placed by Sigereth on what the sorcerer must bet in return, however if the mortal loses through knowing cheating on behalf of anyone else (including the sorcerer, other players, or those peripherally involved) those people take the place of the winnings. As a miscellaneous action, the sorcerer can offer up a won person to Sigereth in exchange for power for one scene, rolling (Essence + Willpower) and gaining that many sorcerous motes. He retains these motes until the end of the scene. Addtionally, a bound soul may be reflexively expended in place of a point of Willpower when paying the cost of the sorcerer's control spell. When won people are spent in either of these ways, they are immediately transported to Sigereth's domain in Malfeas, where they are reshaped into baidaks. Baidaks themselves are specifically exempted from the requirement that the wagering player be mortal; however, they will always insist that the sorcerer wage themselves in return. As usual, compulsions to play or gamble negate the ritual when used on baidaks, including the compulsion inherent in a sorcerous summoning. The sorcerer cannot have more than (Essence + Occult) won people at any one time. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm hoping to get Celestial initiation from Orabilis, but I'm a little way off &amp; I only have vague ideas for merits &amp; rituals. If this is still going when I figure out details I'll add them in.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","user":"Katamari_Naneke","date":".  Something went wrong with the formatting. 03-03-2019, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}